From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: omarchy-asus <noreply@github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] EXPERIMENTAL: crypto: ccp: runtime PM for PSP-only PCI
 functions (ccp.psp_rpm_delay_ms, default off)

EXPERIMENTAL, DEFAULT OFF (local carry for ROG Zephyrus G16 GA605KM idle
power testing; not submitted upstream).

ccp has no runtime PM: the reference the PCI core takes in
local_pci_probe() is never given back, so the PSP function (1022:17E0 on
the G16, 65:00.2) stays in D0 even with power/control at "auto". Windows
idles this function in S0. On the G16, SMU idlemask bit 16 (the runtime
deep-idle blocker) turns idle in s2idle's noirq phase, where the PCI core
moves this function to D3hot; this lets that be tried at runtime.

  ccp.psp_rpm_delay_ms (int, 0644, default 0 = off)

When it is > 0, for a PSP-only PCI function without SEV (no CCP engines,
no SEV vdata), the driver gives up the probe reference and uses
autosuspend with that delay. With power/control at "auto" as well, the
function goes to D3hot once no command has touched its registers for
that long. A write applies at once to bound functions: > 0 drops the
reference (or changes the delay), 0 takes it back and resumes the
function. With 0, or with power/control at "on" (the PCI core's default),
nothing changes.

Every path that touches the function's registers holds a runtime PM
reference, psp_pm_get()/psp_pm_put() (pm_runtime_resume_and_get() and
pm_runtime_put_autosuspend()): the PSP mailbox (psp_mailbox_command(), so
the TEE ring init/destroy, SFS and the extended commands), the TEE ring
commands (psp_tee_process_cmd(), every amdtee and amd-pmf call), platform
access (psp_send_platform_access_msg(), psp_ring_platform_doorbell(),
HSTI), the dbc ioctl and the firmware-version sysfs attributes and their
is_visible(). The reference is taken on these devices whether or not
runtime PM is on, so turning it on or off never unbalances a command in
flight; on every other ccp/PSP device the helpers do nothing. The PSP
interrupt handler is left alone: a function in D3hot cannot raise MSI-X,
and the handler only serves SEV.

The runtime_suspend callback sends the PSP nothing (it has no such
command): pci_pm_runtime_suspend() saves config space and
pci_finish_runtime_suspend() sets D3hot (no ACPI _PS3/_PR3 on the G16's
PSP node), the same register write as s2idle's noirq D3hot, after which
the TEE ring keeps working without a re-init. runtime_resume has nothing
to restore. The system-sleep callbacks are unchanged; without
DPM_FLAG_SMART_SUSPEND the PCI core resumes a runtime-suspended function
before its suspend callback.

  ccp.psp_rpm_debug (bool, 0644, default off)

logs each runtime suspend and resume with a running count, and for a
resume the ccp entry point's caller that woke the function (or "not for a
ccp command": power/control, system sleep, the PCI core), to see who
wakes it.

The fTPM (tpm_crb, CRB at 0xFED40000) and amdgpu's PSP block (MP0
C2PMSG registers through amdgpu's own MMIO BAR) do not use this
function's BARs, so they never resume it; whether the PSP firmware serves
them with its function in D3hot is what the G16 test checks.

Tracked in omarchy-asus #249.
---
diff --git a/drivers/crypto/ccp/dbc.c b/drivers/crypto/ccp/dbc.c
--- a/drivers/crypto/ccp/dbc.c
+++ b/drivers/crypto/ccp/dbc.c
@@ -128,7 +128,7 @@
 	psp->dbc_data = NULL;
 }
 
-static long dbc_ioctl(struct file *filp, unsigned int cmd, unsigned long arg)
+static long __dbc_ioctl(struct file *filp, unsigned int cmd, unsigned long arg)
 {
 	struct psp_device *psp_master = psp_get_master_device();
 	void __user *argp = (void __user *)arg;
@@ -184,6 +184,21 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/* EXPERIMENTAL: one runtime PM reference across the ioctl's commands */
+static long dbc_ioctl(struct file *filp, unsigned int cmd, unsigned long arg)
+{
+	struct psp_device *psp_master = psp_get_master_device();
+	long ret;
+
+	ret = psp_pm_get(psp_master, _RET_IP_);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+	ret = __dbc_ioctl(filp, cmd, arg);
+	psp_pm_put(psp_master);
+
+	return ret;
+}
+
 static const struct file_operations dbc_fops = {
 	.owner	= THIS_MODULE,
 	.unlocked_ioctl = dbc_ioctl,
